.TH "MEDIARECORDER.START_EVENT" "3JS" "October 27, 2026" "JavaScript" "JavaScript Reference Manual"
.SH NAME
MediaRecorder.start_event \- MediaRecorder: start event
.SH SYNOPSIS
The \f[B]\f[CB]start\f[B]\f[R] event of the \f[CR]MediaRecorder\f[R]
interface is fired when \f[CR]MediaRecorder.start()\f[R] is called.
At this point, the data starts being gathered into a \f[CR]Blob\f[R].
.SH SYNTAX
Use the event name in \f[CR]addEventListener()\f[R]:
.IP
.EX
addEventListener(\(dqstart\(dq, (event) => { })
.EE
.PP
Alternatively, assign to the event handler property of the interface:
.IP
.EX
onstart = (event) => { }
.EE
.SH EVENT TYPE
A generic \f[CR]Event\f[R].
.SH EXAMPLE
.IP
.EX
record.onclick = () \f[B]=>\f[R] {
  mediaRecorder.start();
  console.log(\(dqrecorder started\(dq);
};

mediaRecorder.onstart = () \f[B]=>\f[R] {
  \f[I]// do something in response to\f[R]
  \f[I]// recording being started\f[R]
};
.EE
